autoresearch (ccplugins) — a skill-only autonomous experiment loop.

This work re-implements protocol behaviour derived from prior MIT-licensed
projects:

  • drivelineresearch/autoresearch-claude-code (MIT) — noise-floor gating, the
    METRIC name=number contract, MAD confidence, locked eval harness, checks
    gate, budget caps, and JSONL + git-branch winner tracking.
  • wjgoarxiv/autoresearch-skill (MIT) — file-based state model, the
    {"pass": bool, "score": number} evaluator contract, multi-level plateau
    pivots, and cross-agent portability idioms.
  • uditgoenka/autoresearch (MIT) — the thin-router + lazy-loaded reference-file
    architecture adopted for context economy.

Ultimately inspired by karpathy/autoresearch.

Behaviour was re-implemented from the described protocols; no source files were
copied from any of the above.

